---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PlatformIcon from '../components/PlatformIcon';
import { CHALLENGE_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_URL, REPO_URL, SQUIDMAPS_URL, YEAR, withBase } from '../lib/site';

const link = 'font-semibold text-ink-600 underline decoration-ink-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300';
---

<Layout
  title={`About · #30DayMapChallenge ${YEAR} Gallery`}
  description="How the #30DayMapChallenge gallery collects maps, why it only includes Bluesky and Mastodon, and how we respect privacy settings."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-10 pb-4 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
    <p class="font-display text-sm font-extrabold tracking-widest text-ink-500 uppercase">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">A simple, open gallery of challenge maps</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
      Every November, thousands of maps are shared for the <a class={link} href={CHALLENGE_URL}>#30DayMapChallenge</a>, started by
      <a class={link} href="https://tjukanov.org/">Topi Tjukanov</a>. They're scattered across feeds and gone in a scroll. This gallery collects
      them by day so you can browse every take on every theme. It's built and hosted by <a class={link} href={SQUIDMAPS_URL}>squidmaps</a> as a community resource.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
      <section id="included" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">How to be included</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">There's nothing to submit. The gallery checks for new posts every 6 hours and picks a map up automatically when its post:</p>
        <ol class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {[
            ['Is on Bluesky or Mastodon', 'and visible to everyone.'],
            ['Uses #30DayMapChallenge', 'in the post text.'],
            ['Says which day', 'such as "Day 12", "#day12", "12/30", or the theme hashtag, e.g. #hexagons.'],
            ['Includes the map as an image', 'The first image becomes the tile.'],
          ].map(([title, body], i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:ring-zinc-800">
              <span class="grid size-7 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ink-500 font-display text-sm font-black text-white">{i + 1}</span>
              <span><span class="font-semibold">{title}</span> <span class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">{body}</span></span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-500">Posting on both platforms is fine: cross-posts are merged into one tile that links to each copy.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="why" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Why only Bluesky and Mastodon?</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 flex gap-2 text-zinc-500" aria-hidden="true">
          <PlatformIcon platform="bluesky" className="size-6" />
          <PlatformIcon platform="mastodon" className="size-6" />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">We wanted a gallery that's simple to run, fair to everyone, and respectful of people's choices. One clear rule does that better than a submission queue:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          <li><strong>Open, public data.</strong> Both platforms have free, documented APIs for public posts. There's no scraping, no paid access, and no logging in as someone else.</li>
          <li><strong>Clear privacy settings we can honor.</strong> Both let people say "don't show my posts this way," and we can check that automatically (see below).</li>
          <li><strong>Easy to moderate.</strong> Instead of reviewing a stream of submissions, we include whatever is public and tagged, and step in only when something's wrong. That keeps a free side project running.</li>
          <li><strong>Links that work for everyone.</strong> Every tile opens the original post, and anyone can view it without an account.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
          LinkedIn, X, Instagram and Threads don't offer open access to public posts for a project like this. We can't include them consistently or respectfully,
          so we don't include them at all. If you post there too, cross-post a copy to Bluesky or Mastodon to be included.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Privacy and what we store</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          <li><strong>We skip people who've opted out.</strong> That means Bluesky accounts that hide their posts from logged-out viewers, and Mastodon accounts set to hide from search engines or to stay out of discovery. These settings are re-checked every day, so changing one takes effect within a day.</li>
          <li><strong>We don't copy your images.</strong> Tiles load the picture straight from Bluesky or your Mastodon server. We only keep the link, the author's name and handle, and the start of the post text.</li>
          <li><strong>Deleted posts disappear here too.</strong> A deleted post's image stops loading right away, and the post is removed from the gallery within a day.</li>
          <li><strong>Maps belong to their creators.</strong> We're just pointing to them.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-2xl bg-ink-50 p-6 sm:p-8 dark:bg-ink-700/20">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Missing a map, or want yours removed?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          First check the list above. Most missing maps don't say which day they're for. If it still isn't showing up, or you'd like your work taken out of the gallery,
          email <a class={link} href={CONTACT_URL}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with a link to the post and we'll sort it out by hand.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
          The gallery is open source: see the code <a class={link} href={REPO_URL}>on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href={withBase('/')} class="inline-flex rounded-full bg-ink-500 px-5 py-2.5 font-bold text-white hover:bg-ink-600">Browse the gallery →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
